#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
omodel-manager

Manage the vLLM Docker containers you launch on your GPU box: see what's
running, stop one, and launch new ones from an editable config file.

Design:
  * Launch definitions live in a SEPARATE, editable JSON config (not in this
    script): model_manager.json next to this script by default (override with
    --config PATH or $OTOOLS_MODEL_MANAGER_CONFIG).
    On first run the file is created, pre-seeded with a working Qwen3.6 profile.
  * Containers launched here are tagged with docker labels (otools.manager,
    otools.model, otools.port) and a predictable name (otools-vllm-<key>), so
    `ps` / `stop` / `logs` only ever touch containers this tool started.
  * The docker command is assembled as an argv list and run WITHOUT a shell,
    so values like --speculative-config '{"method":"mtp",...}' need no quoting.
  * HF_TOKEN: taken from $HF_TOKEN if set, else the store `install` writes at
    ~/.config/otools/hf_token (0600). Locally it's passed as `-e HF_TOKEN`
    (inherited, keeps it out of argv); for remote it's forwarded by value.
    `install` checks for it and, with --fix, prompts with steps to create one.
  * REMOTE: with --host ALIAS|USER@HOST (or defaults.remote / per-model remote in
    config) every docker call runs on that box over SSH. Bind-mount paths resolve
    against the REMOTE $HOME, declared assets are scp'd over, HF_TOKEN is forwarded
    from your local shell, and `health` targets the remote host. `install` bootstraps
    the box (keyless SSH, docker install, docker group) -- run it first. It uses a
    dedicated, clearly-named key (~/.ssh/otools_model_manager_ed25519, comment
    "otools_model_manager@<laptop>") and pins it (-i + IdentitiesOnly) so the tool's
    access is self-contained and easy to revoke later.

Stdlib only. Commands:
  omodel-manager install user@192.0.2.101 dgx1 --fix   # bootstrap + name a host
  omodel-manager --... launch <key> --host dgx1
  omodel-manager ps                 # running managed containers (default)
  omodel-manager ps --all           # also list other vllm/* containers
  omodel-manager models             # profiles defined in the config file
  omodel-manager launch qwen3.6     # launch a profile (detached)
  omodel-manager launch qwen3.6 --dry-run     # print docker cmd, don't run
  omodel-manager launch qwen3.6 --foreground  # run -it instead of -d
  omodel-manager fetch nemotron-3-super-120b-nvfp4   # pre-download its assets
  omodel-manager stop qwen3.6       # stop+remove (alias: kill)
  omodel-manager logs qwen3.6 -f    # follow container logs
  omodel-manager health             # GET /v1/models on each running one
  omodel-manager config --path|--init|--edit
"""

